---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Wait until a run is ready or complete.

--until sets the status to wait for:
  ready     The run is ready to use, or it is already complete.
  complete  The run is complete: completed, cancelled, or incomplete. This
            is the default.

The status is a minimum. A run can only move forward, and a complete run never
starts again. Thus `--until ready` on a complete run returns at once.

When the run reaches the status, the command prints the run's current status and
succeeds, whatever that status is. A run that reports status `unknown` fails the
command: snouty cannot tell whether such a run will still make progress.

The wait is unbounded unless --timeout is given. The command is safe to
interrupt and re-run: it holds no state beyond the run id.

--timeout and --poll-interval take h/m/s units, in that order, such as 90s, 5m
or 1h30m. A bare number counts minutes.

Examples:
  snouty runs wait <run_id>
  snouty runs wait <run_id> --timeout 2h
  snouty runs wait <run_id> --until ready
  snouty launch --json --config ./config ... | jq -r .runId | xargs snouty runs
  wait

Add --json for machine-readable output. The final status prints as one JSON
object:
  snouty --json runs wait <run_id> | jq -r .status

Usage: snouty runs wait [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

Options:
      --poll-interval <POLL_INTERVAL>
          Time between status checks, at least 1 minute (e.g. 90s, 5m). A bare
          number counts minutes
          
          [default: 1m]

      --timeout <TIMEOUT>
          Give up after this long (e.g. 2h); without it the wait is unbounded. A
          bare number counts minutes

      --until <UNTIL>
          The status to wait for; a later status also ends the wait

          Possible values:
          - ready:    The run is ready to use, or already complete
          - complete: The run is completed, cancelled, or incomplete
          
          [default: complete]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
